# wawona.io voice

Applies to all public copy, docs, templates, and UI strings in this repo.

## Dashes

Never use an em dash (Unicode U+2014, `&mdash;`, `&#8212;`). Never use an en dash as a stand-in between words.

Use a period, comma, colon, or parentheses. Numeric ranges use a hyphen: `5-15 GB`.

```text
Bad:  Native on macOS — no VM.
Good: Native on macOS. No VM.

Bad:  Fastlane — lanes in fastlane/
Good: Fastlane: lanes in fastlane/
```

The Bad lines above are the only place this glyph may appear: so the agent can match it. Never put it in site copy.

## Sound like a person

Write short sentences. Say the thing. Do not sell.

Avoid: seamless, robust, leverage, utilize, delve, unlock (metaphor), empower, cutting-edge, next-generation, from the ground up, designed from day one, it's important to note, in order to, simply, effortlessly, revolutionary, catalyst, frontier, orchestrate, monolithic, first-class citizen, the future of.

Avoid three-beat marketing lists ("No X, no Y, no Z") unless they are three product facts.

Avoid fake gravitas on buttons and headings ("Forge the Source", "Enter the Discussion", "Fuel the Vision", "Built Different"). Use "GitHub", "Discord", "Support".

```text
Bad:  We are bringing high-performance, bare-metal Wayland execution to the hardware where it was previously impossible.
Good: Wawona is a native Wayland compositor for Mac, iPhone, and Android. No VM.
```
